{
  "message": "Good news: the local check passed for design revision 2. It ran with no failures or blockers, so the private bucket contract works as expected against an S3-compatible emulator. That emulator isn't IBM COS, though, so IBM IAM, the endpoints and the region are still unchecked, and the biggest open gap is where the data is allowed to live. Which country must these synthetic documents stay in? For example Australia, which would support au-syd, or \"no restriction\".",
